---
description: How to run things
alwaysApply: true
---

**The full execution sequence is in `CURSOR_START.md`.** Prefer `make` over hand-typed commands; the targets carry the arguments that make runs
comparable (seeds, depth lists, prompt version, output directory).

```
make check        # preflight + pytest + ruff   <- run before trusting anything
make data         # Arm 1 counts (fills the Section 3 brackets) + Arm 2 item set
make run-offline  # both arms, diagnostic models, no API key
make run-llm      # depth sweep + Arm 1 under prompt v2 (needs OPENAI_API_KEY)
make paper        # regenerate results/PAPER_DATA.md
make verify       # diff the manuscript against the artifacts; non-zero on drift
make finish       # the whole deterministic chain
```

Nothing except `run-llm` needs a key or a network connection. The committed snapshot makes
both arms reproducible offline.

Two gates that must stay green: `make verify` (the paper cannot drift from its data) and
`scripts/preflight.py` (the installation actually works). Both run in CI.

Do not add a number to a results file, the README or the paper by hand. `make paper`
generates them; if a figure is missing, the collector prints the command that fills it.
